    <l n="1" para="true">2. Noxalis actio personalis est, sed in rem scripta.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">3. Noxa dare non tenetur dominus.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Quid significet vocabulum noxa, &amp;</l>
    <l n="5">noxia.</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Noxales actiones aequitate nituntur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">1. <i>Dominus servum noxa dando ejus dominium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>amittit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">2. <i>Multis in casibus noxalis cessat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">3. <i>Servus si damnum sua pecunia resarci-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>at, fit liber.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Origo noxalium actionum describitur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Noxalis actio sequitur caput &amp; datur</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>in quemcunque servi possessorem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">1. <i>Cessat noxalis, quando servus domino</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>noxiam dat vel dedit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">2. <i>Quid jure Hebraeorum obtineat?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">3. <i>Quid moribus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 4. INSTIT. TIT. 9.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Si quadrupes pauperiem fecisse dicatur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">1. NOxalis servorum differt a noxali</l>
    <l n="28">quadrupedum.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">2. <i>Quid fiat, si animal algrum alterius de-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>pascat?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31" para="true">3. <i>In homine libero vulnerato deformita-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32">
      <i>tis non est habenda ratio.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="33" para="true">4. <i>Actio de pauperie vel directa vel utilis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34" para="true">5. <i>Quid si canis damnum dederit?</i> §. 1.</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">1. Praeter actionem de pauperie datur</l>
    <l n="36">alia ex edicto aedilium.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">2. Plures actiones poenales concurrere possunt.</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">3. Jus Hebraeorum enarratur.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">4. Mores allegantur.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">5. Etiam jus feudale.</l>
    <l n="41" type="heading" level="1" caput="10" para="true">LIBR. 4. INSTIT. TIT. 10.</l>
    <l n="42" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De iis per quos agere possumus.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">1. Olim nemo per procuratorem,</l>
    <l n="44">nisi in certis casibus litigare pote-</l>
    <l n="45">rat.</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">1. Quomodo constituatur procurator.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">2. Quotuplex sit mandatum?</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">3. Quibus in casibus speciale mandatum</l>
    <l n="51">desideretur?</l>
    <l n="52" para="true">4. Quid moribus?</l>
